<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.8.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00194</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.8.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>1f1a0820-17e0-4450-aa22-8ac35c2d3aed</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>

<para>For 1 - 4 use the problem below:</para>


<blockquote>
  Priya is buying raisins and almonds to make trail mix. Almonds cost $5.20 per pound and raisins cost $2.75 per
  pound. Priya spent $11.70 buying almonds and raisins. The relationship between pounds of almonds, pounds of
    raisins, and the total cost is represented by the equation \(5.2a+2.75r=11.7\).
</blockquote>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="4925ec3f-3e0b-4441-a6d1-e247f6dd0a33" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Enter Questions Below this line-->

  <!--Q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="141ee309-47d6-4ef8-a902-faf57beecc60" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="0.473" data-solution-options="[&quot;1.192&quot;, &quot;2.75&quot;, &quot;0.946&quot;, &quot;0.473&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>How many pounds of raisins did Priya buy if she bought the following amount of almonds:</para>
      <para>2 pounds of almonds</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 0.473</para>
      <para>\(5.2(2) + 2.75r = 11.7\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="aa71602e-9229-4eea-a6a2-8eb5dfac8752" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="2.25" data-solution-options="[&quot;2.25&quot;, &quot;1.689&quot;, &quot;5.5&quot;, &quot;2.811&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>1.06 pounds of almonds</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 2.25 </para>
      <para>\(5.2(1.06) + 2.75r = 11.7\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="2ecb1097-cef5-424f-938a-28c3ab6edf15" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="3.044" data-solution-options="[&quot;9.94&quot;, &quot;1.911&quot;, &quot;3.044&quot;,&quot;8.371&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>0.64 pounds of almonds</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 3.044</para>
      <para>\(5.2(0.64) + 2.75r = 11.7\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="04e4c308-5efd-4fe9-b71d-e10a46997b05" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(r=\frac{11.7-5.2a}{2.75}\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(r=\\frac{11.7+5.2a}{275}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(r=\\frac{11.7-2.75a}{5.2}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(r=\\frac{2.75}{11.7-5.2a}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(r=\\frac{11.7-5.2a}{2.75}\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(a\) pounds of almonds</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(r=\frac{1.7-5.2a}{2.75}\)</para>
      <para>\(5.2(a) + 2.75r = 11.7\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="b5b4af86-a741-4892-a2a9-94abd8e233ed" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="36" data-solution-options="[&quot;40&quot;, &quot;80&quot;, &quot;36&quot;, &quot;60&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>For 5 - 6 use the problem below:</para>
      <blockquote>A car traveled 180 miles at a constant rate.</blockquote>
      <para> For each of the missing spaces in the table, a-d, select the missing value that
          completes the table to show the rate at which the car was traveling if it
          completed the same distance in each number of hours.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
              Travel Time</entry>
            <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
              Rate of Travel</entry>
          </row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>5</entry>
            <entry>a. ____ </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>4.5</entry>
            <entry>b. ____ </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>3</entry>
            <entry>c. ____ </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>2.25</entry>
            <entry>d. ____ </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <para>   a.______</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 36</para>
      <para>\(\frac{180}{5}=36\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="949cd5c8-e172-4c75-9046-f688c03bbaba" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="40" data-solution-options="[&quot;40&quot;, &quot;80&quot;, &quot;36&quot;, &quot;60&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>   b. _____</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 40</para>
      <para>\(\frac{180}{4.5}=40\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="ed99f41d-13e6-4be7-b1ba-e786dd1d841c" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="60" data-solution-options="[&quot;40&quot;, &quot;80&quot;, &quot;36&quot;, &quot;60&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>   c. _____</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 60</para>
      <para>\(\frac{180}{3}=60\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e46a957b-f722-4e79-acb0-5917929b9c84" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="80" data-solution-options="[&quot;40&quot;, &quot;80&quot;, &quot;36&quot;, &quot;60&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>   d. _____</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 80</para>
      <para>\(\frac{180}{2.25}=80\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="0d45981e-3d0c-4b99-9426-0f75365c3047" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(r=\frac{180}t\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(r=\\frac t{180}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(r=\\frac{180}t\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(r=180t\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(r-180-t\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Choose the equation that would make it easy to find the rate at which the car
          was traveling in miles per hour \(r\), if it traveled for \(t\) hours.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(r=\frac{180}t\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q10-->
  <exercise data-content-id="48e38499-b2ca-4eb1-ba5e-2bb72198961b" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;3 bananas and 2 apples&quot;, &quot;1 banana and 3 apples&quot;, &quot;5 bananas and 1 apple&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;2 bananas and 2 apples&quot;, &quot;3 bananas and 2 apples&quot;, &quot;1 banana and 2 apples&quot;, &quot;1 banana and 3 apples&quot;, &quot;5 bananas and 2 apples&quot;, &quot;5 bananas and 1 apple&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Bananas cost $0.50 each, and apples cost $1.00 each. <emphasis>Select all three</emphasis> combinations of bananas
          and apples that Elena could buy for exactly $3.50.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 3 bananas and 2 apples,1 banana and 3 apples, 5 bananas and 1 apple</para>
      <para>\(3(0.5)+2(1)=3.50\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q11-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e41358fd-8187-4c65-b531-f0ea183aee73" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(t=\frac{A-P}{Pr}\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(t=\\frac{P-A}{Pr}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(t=\\frac{A-P}{Pr}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(t=\\frac{A+P}{Pr}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(t=\\frac{r(A-P)}P\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Choose the best answer to solve the formula \(A=P+Prt\) for \(t\).</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(t=\frac{A-P}{Pr}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.8.2.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
